---
title: Standing Upper Back Stretch 
type: docs
prev: docs/rastyazhka/
---
![выгибание спины](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07f345cd-e0fb-44f5-b4fe-7f17d9ce8c41)

{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Stand up straight, interlace your fingers in front of your chest, and turn your palms outward facing away from you.

### Step 2
Lower your chin toward your chest and gently round your upper back to stretch your shoulders and upper back muscles.

### Step 3
Reach your hands forward away from your body until you feel a pleasant stretch between your shoulder blades.

### Step 4
Hold this position for the recommended amount of time (usually 15–30 seconds).

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Try to keep the target muscles relaxed during the stretch.

• Breathe slowly and steadily.

• Do not force the stretch—stretch only until you feel comfortable tension, never sharp pain.
{{< /callout >}}
